  <h3>How to apply</h3>
  <ol class="net-steps" role="list">
    <li><strong>Register</strong> online with your own email address and mobile number.</li>
    <li><strong>Fill in the application form.</strong> Upload your live photograph, a recent photograph and your signature. PwD / PwBD candidates also upload a disability or UDID certificate.</li>
    <li><strong>Pay the fee</strong> online by net banking, debit card, credit card or UPI. Then download and keep the confirmation page. It is made only after the payment succeeds.</li>
  </ol>
  <ul>
    <li>You can apply <strong>online only</strong>, on the official NTA website. Do not send any document to NTA by post, fax, WhatsApp, email or by hand.</li>
    <li>Use your own email address and mobile number. NTA sends important messages only to them.</li>
    <li>Check every detail. NTA does not change the details you submit, apart from the correction window.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="net-reading net-anchor" id="net-about-preparation" aria-labelledby="net-about-preparation-h">
  <h2 id="net-about-preparation-h">How to work through the subject</h2>
  <p>Use the syllabus as a checklist, and give reading, practice and revision their own place in your plan.</p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Start with chronology.</strong> Read the history of English literature age by age, from Old English to the present. A timeline helps you place writers, works and movements.</li>
    <li><strong>Make room for criticism and theory early.</strong> Return to these topics in short, regular revision sessions.</li>
    <li><strong>Keep Paper 1 in your plan.</strong> Work on teaching, research, reasoning and comprehension alongside your English reading.</li>
    <li><strong>Use previous-year questions to diagnose gaps.</strong> Separate an unfamiliar fact from a misread question, then revise accordingly.</li>
    <li><strong>Revise in cycles.</strong> Keep condensed notes and return to them instead of treating a unit as finished after one reading.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="net-source-note">Source: the NTA Information Bulletin for UGC-NET December 2026 (updated 16 October 2026), and NTA public notices of 27 October, 1 November and 2 November 2026. <a href="https://ugcnet.nta.nic.in/information-bulletin/" rel="noopener">Read the official NTA information bulletins</a>. For questions about the exam, contact the NTA helpdesk on 011-40759000 or at ugcnet@nta.ac.in.</p>
